00:31:08.000 --> 00:32:07.000
Approximately three hours later, Regan Trethway heard a strange noise. He looked out the front window of his house and saw a blonde woman trying to open his front door. It was Cindy made peace. She mouthed some words to him and was about to lose consciousness. As she pointed to her throat, Regan could make out a black stocking tied tightly around her neck. He cut the ligature with difficulty as it was so tight he couldn't get his fingers under it. Treating doctors at the University of BC Hospital Emergency Department did not know what to make of the attack. Cindy had puffy red eyes from being strangled, a bloody left nostril and a sore right ankle. Ozzie Caban had met Cindy at Regan Trethway's before she was transported by ambulance.
大约三个小时后，雷根·特雷思韦（Regan Trethway）听到了一种奇怪的声音。他望向自己家的前窗，看到一个金发女子正试图打开他的前门。那是辛迪·梅克皮斯。她对他说着无声的话，眼看就要失去知觉。当她指着自己的喉咙时，雷根辨认出一条黑色长筒袜紧紧缠绕在她的脖子上。他费力地割断了勒带，因为它勒得太紧，他的手指根本塞不进去。不列颠哥伦比亚大学医院急诊科的主治医生们不知道该如何应对这起袭击。辛迪因为被勒而充血红肿，左鼻孔流血，右脚踝疼痛。奥齐·卡班在辛迪被救护车运走之前，在雷根·特雷思韦家见到了她。

31
00:32:07.000 --> 00:33:08.000
He informed the doctors of two fresh needle puncture marks he had seen on Cindy's inner elbow. Toxicology tests were run which showed the presence of benzodiazepines in Cindy's bloodstream, but did not give a result as to the concentration of drugs in her system. When they undressed her, nursing staff found twigs and leaves in her underwear. Cindy's recollection of events was hazy. She didn't remember anything after giving the man in the van directions. The next thing she recalled was speaking to a doctor in the hospital. A search of Dunbar Park where Cindy was abducted located one of her shoes, the canister of dog repellent she carried for protection with a drag mark in the dirt about 10 meters from the sidewalk where the van pulled up.
他向医生通报了他在辛迪内肘处看到的两个新鲜针孔。医院进行了毒理学测试，结果显示辛迪的血液中存在苯二氮䓬类药物，但未测出其体内的药物浓度。当护理人员脱掉她的衣服时，在她的内衣里发现了树枝和树叶。辛迪对事件的记忆有些模糊。在给面包车里的男人指路后，她什么也不记得了。她记忆中的下一件事就是在医院里和医生说话。对辛迪被绑架的邓巴公园（Dunbar Park）的搜查找到了她的一只鞋、她随身携带用于防身的小罐狗驱虫剂，在离面包车停下的马路边约 10 米处的泥土里还有一道拖曳痕迹。

32
00:33:08.000 --> 00:34:00.000
Later that evening in the emergency department, clerk Lisa Latimore received a call. The call was received directly at the emergency desk by passing the hospital switchboard system. A man on the line asked, do you have hospital security? When Lisa asked him to clarify what he meant, the man replied, do you have security guards? He also asked what time the emergency department closed. The perplexed clerk advised the man that it didn't close. He went on to ask how many floors the hospital had. Not wanting to divulge any further information, Lisa told the man she would transfer him to her supervisor.
那天晚上晚些时候在急诊室，文员丽莎·拉蒂莫尔（Lisa Latimore）接到了一个电话。这通电话是直接打到急诊前台的，绕过了医院的总机系统。线上的一个男人问：“你们有医院保安吗？”当丽莎请他澄清他的意思时，该男子回答说：“你们有保安吗？”他还问急诊室几点关门。这位困惑的文员告诉该男子急诊室是24小时不关门的。接着他又问医院有多少层。丽莎不想透露更多信息，便告诉该男子她会把他转接给主管。

33
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:57.000
The man abruptly hung up. Lisa reported the unusual call to Detective David Boyer Smith who was at the hospital interviewing Cindy Makepeace. She told him that the caller had a strange accent, possibly of South African or New Zealand extraction. In an attempt to remember details of the past attacks, Cindy agreed to undergo sessions of hypnosis. In the book about Cindy Makepeace by Neil Hall, the sessions were successful. Cindy was able to recall from the latest attack the model of the van that it had chrome mirrors, a rubber pad on the bumper and a smoky coloured air vent on top. She recalled being dragged into the van which had carpeting in the back and several people inside.
该男子挂断了电话。丽莎将这通不同寻常的电话报告给了正在医院采访辛迪·梅克皮斯的侦探大卫·博耶·史密斯。她告诉他，来电者有一种奇怪的口音，可能是南非或新西兰口音。为了尝试回忆过去袭击的细节，辛迪同意接受催眠治疗。在尼尔·霍尔（Neil Hall）所著的关于辛迪·梅克皮斯的书中，这些治疗很成功。辛迪能够从最近的一次袭击中回忆起那辆面包车的型号：它有镀铬后视镜、保险杠上有橡胶垫，顶部有一个烟灰色的通风口。她回忆起自己被拖进了一辆面包车，车后面铺着地毯，里面有几个人。

34
00:34:57.000 --> 00:35:54.000
One had a mask and a wig on. She felt a sharp prick on her arm and a voice surrounding her. One of the voices uttered the word hombergosh. Cindy explained that this was a South African Zulu word that translated to be warned, do as I say. Roy Makepeace was South African and spoke with a strong accent. At the third hypnosis session held on October 2, Cindy made a startling revelation. She recalled a trip that she and Roy had taken on board the peacemaker just over three years earlier in July 1981. They had sailed to an isolated area of the Gulf Islands, approximately 75 kilometres from Vancouver.
其中一个人戴着面具和假发。她感到手臂上被刺了一下，周围响起了说话声。其中一个声音吐出了“hombergosh”这个词。辛迪解释说，这是一个南非祖鲁语单词，翻译过来就是“当心，照我说的做”。罗伊·梅特皮斯是南非人，说话带有浓重的口音。在 10 月 2 日举行的第三次催眠治疗中，辛迪有了一个惊人的发现。她回想起三年多前的 1981 年 7 月，她和罗伊乘坐“和平缔造者”号进行的一次旅行。他们航行到了海湾群岛（Gulf Islands）的一个偏远地区，距离温哥华大约 75 公里。

35
00:35:54.000 --> 00:36:48.000
As they tied up to the wharf, Cindy decided to stay below and take a nap while Roy went to look at some property on the island. Becoming visibly distressed during the hypnosis session, Cindy recounted how she heard some shouting. After putting on her jeans and shoes, she went above deck and shouted back. No one responded. She investigated the noise, happening upon a log cabin further inland at the top of a hill. She approached the front porch. Firewood was stacked neatly to one side. Cindy knocked on the door, but there was no answer. She cautiously opened the door to see Roy Makepeace standing there.
当他们把船系在码头上时，辛迪决定留在船舱下面打个盹，而罗伊则去岛上看一些房产。在催眠治疗中表现出明显的痛苦，辛迪讲述了她听到一些喊叫声的过程。穿上牛仔裤和鞋子后，她走到甲板上并大声喊回去。没有人回应。她去查明噪音的来源，偶然发现了一个位于内陆小山顶上的木屋。她走近前廊。一侧整齐地堆放着木柴。辛迪敲了敲门，但无人应答。她小心翼翼地推开门，看到罗伊·梅特皮斯正站在那里。

36
00:36:48.000 --> 00:37:43.000
He was very angry. On the floor were the bodies of two people, a man in his 30s and a woman in her 20s. Roy was holding a knife. It was covered in blood. Running from the cabin, Cindy screamed out to Roy that he was a murderer and vomited. Roy caught up to Cindy, slapped her on the face and shook her. The next thing she remembered was sitting on a bed while Roy hacked the bodies into pieces with an axe to dispose of in the ocean. From the book by Neil Hall, Cindy told the hypnotherapist, I don't know how I got there. I'm just sitting on the bed. I'm numb as if in a shell.
他非常生气。地板上躺着两具尸体，一个 30 多岁的男人和一个 20 多岁的女人。罗伊手里拿着一把刀。刀上沾满了血。辛迪从木屋里跑出来，尖叫着对罗伊说他是个杀人犯，并吐了。罗伊追上辛迪，扇了她耳光并摇晃她。她记忆中的下一件事就是坐在床边，看着罗伊用斧头将尸体剁成碎块以便扔进大海。根据尼尔·霍尔的书，辛迪对催眠治疗师说：“我不知道我是怎么到那里的。我只是坐在床上。我麻木得就像在一个空壳里。”

37
00:37:43.000 --> 00:38:44.000
But part of me is screaming inside. Detectives attempted to pinpoint the cabin that Cindy had described in her hypnotherapy sessions. It was a difficult task given that Cindy was asleep when they docked and didn't know where the cabin was located in the vast expanse of the Gulf Islands. Although she could recall the interior with clarity, a rough wooden floor, great blanket, a wooden cupboard stacked with books, an old table that had writing paper on it, a wood stove and maps on the wall. The exterior offered no distinguishing features. The Royal Canadian Mounted Police searched the area described by Cindy for a full day but could not locate the cabin. Employing another tactic, Cindy agreed to call her husband using a phone that was tapped by police.
“但我的内心有一部分在尖叫。”侦探们试图精确确定辛迪在催眠治疗中描述的小屋。这是一项艰巨的任务，因为辛迪靠岸时正在睡觉，并且不知道在广袤的海湾群岛中那间小屋的具体位置。尽管她能清晰地回忆起内部陈设：粗糙的木地板、灰色的毯子、堆满书的木橱柜、一张放着信纸的旧桌子、一个燃木炉以及墙上的地图。但外观没有任何明显的特征。加拿大皇家骑警在辛迪描述的地区搜查了一整天，但没有找到那间小屋。采取了另一种策略后，辛迪同意使用被警方窃听的电话给她的丈夫打电话。

38
00:38:44.000 --> 00:39:32.000
On July 2, 1985, Roy made Peace's telephone ring. He was surprised to hear Cindy on the other line. They had not spoken since he found out she thought him responsible for the attacks. She began the conversation. With the help of hypnosis, I've been able to remember a lot of why things are happening and what happened four years ago. I wanted to talk to you before letting the police know that I now remember everything. Roy listened as Cindy recounted the bodies in the log cabin. He sounded shocked and angry when she told him she believed he was responsible for the attacks on her and denied any wrongdoing,
1985 年 7 月 2 日，罗伊·梅特皮斯的电话响了。听到听筒那头是辛迪，他感到很惊讶。自从他发现她认为他是袭击事件的幕后黑手以来，他们就再也没有说过话。她开始了对话。在催眠的帮助下，我能够回想起很多事情发生的原因以及四年前发生的事。在让警方知道我现在想通了一切之前，我想和你谈谈。罗伊听着辛迪叙述木屋里的尸体。当辛迪告诉他，她相信他对针对她的袭击事件负有责任时，他听起来既震惊又愤怒，并否认了任何不当行为，

39
00:39:32.000 --> 00:40:24.000
telling Cindy he had nothing to do with it. As she terminated the call, Cindy said, We both know that you have been doing it. I'm not going to listen to that garbage anymore. Immediately following the call, Cindy and Roy Makepeace were placed on round the clock surveillance. This was ceased five days later due to the expense and resources required. During this time, Roy made no attempt to contact or harm Cindy. Six months later, on December 11, Cindy left work on her lunch break and didn't return. That night, Desiree El-Zesa was cycling near the University of British Columbia.
告诉辛迪他对此一无所知。就在她挂断电话时，辛迪说：“我们都知道你一直在这么做。我再也不会听这些鬼话了。”通话结束后不久，辛迪和罗伊·梅克皮斯（Roy Makepeace）受到了全天候监控。由于所需的费用和资源，这项监控在五天后停止。在此期间，罗伊没有试图联系或伤害辛迪。六个月后的12月11日，辛迪在午休时离开工作岗位，没有返回。那天晚上，黛西雷·埃尔-泽萨（Desiree El-Zesa）正在不列颠哥伦比亚大学附近骑自行车。

40
00:40:24.000 --> 00:41:17.000
It was freezing cold as she rode along West 16th Avenue. The December sun had well and truly set by 6.20 as Desiree came to the intersection of Blanca Street. She stopped when something caught her eye. A blonde woman staggered before falling into a ditch across the street. Racing over to her, Desiree noticed the woman had a black stocking wrapped tightly around her neck. She managed to tear the stocking off with her bare hands and called an ambulance. When paramedics arrived, they found Cindy Makepeace standing in the ditch dazed with icy cold water up to her thighs. She was wearing regular clothes with the addition of a black rubber industrial glove on her right hand.
当她沿着西第16大道骑行时，天气冷得结冰。当黛西雷来到布兰卡街（Blanca Street）交叉口时，12月的太阳早已完全落山。当有什么东西吸引了她的目光时，她停了下来。一个金发女郎摇摇晃晃地走着，然后倒在了街对面的沟里。黛西雷跑过去，发现这个女人的脖子上紧紧缠着一只黑色长筒袜。她设法用双手扯下长筒袜并叫了救护车。当护理人员到达时，他们发现辛迪·梅克皮斯正茫然地站在沟里，冰冷的水没到了大腿。她穿着便服，右手戴着一只黑色橡胶工业手套。

41
00:41:17.000 --> 00:42:20.000
One of her feet was bare, the other had on a man's work boot. Concerned about hypothermia, a paramedic coaxed Cindy out of the water and worked on warming her as he took her to the University of BC Hospital. Cindy had scratches on her upper chest, arms, legs and back that looked like they were caused from fingernails or tree branches. She had a dark bruise to her forehead. There was a fresh puncture wound to Cindy's right elbow, indicating that she had been drugged. Blood testing showed the presence of benzodiazepines in her bloodstream. However, Cindy also told the treating doctor she had taken 6 milligrams of the drug Adavan for anxiety earlier in the day. As with previous attacks, Cindy couldn't remember what had happened to her, only events before and after.
她一只脚赤脚，另一只脚穿着男式工作靴。出于对低体温症的担心，一名护理人员劝辛迪走出水面，并在将她送往不列颠哥伦比亚大学医院的途中为她保暖。辛迪的上胸部、手臂、腿和背部有抓痕，看起来像是指甲或树枝造成的。她的前额有一处深色瘀伤。辛迪的右肘有一个新鲜的针刺伤口，表明她被下药了。血液检测显示她的血液中含有苯二氮卓类药物。然而，辛迪也告诉主治医生，她当天早些时候为了焦虑服用了6毫克的阿蒂万（Adavan）。与之前的袭击一样，辛迪记不清自己身上发生了什么，只记得事发前后的事情。

42
00:42:20.000 --> 00:43:28.000
She recalled leaving Blenheim House for lunch and driving to the chemist to pick up her prescription for Adavan. The next thing she recalled was going to the hospital in the ambulance, although she had a vague memory of having her hands tied behind her in an unfamiliar room. Cindy poured her feelings out in her personal diary. She wrote, I don't know why it bothers me so much that I can still only remember bits and pieces of what happened the last time I was attacked. I don't know which is worse, remembering or not being able to remember. I think it would be better if I had total amnesia about it, although it feels so helpless to know things were done to you and you don't know what they were. The police reaction was so confusing. If nothing else, I learned not to talk to anyone about it. Cindy returned to work shortly after the attack, but the experience had a profound effect on her.
她回忆起离开布伦海姆大楼（Blenheim House）吃午饭，开车去药房取阿蒂万的处方药。她接下来回忆的事就是坐救护车去医院，尽管她依稀记得在某个陌生房间里双手被反绑在身后。辛迪在个人日记中倾诉了自己的感受。她写道：“我不知道为什么我还是只能记起上次被袭击时发生的事情的零星片段，这让我如此烦恼。我不知道是记得还是记不清哪个更糟糕。我想如果我对这件事完全失忆会更好，尽管明知道事情发生在你身上却不知道是什么感觉是如此无助。警察的反应太令人困惑了。不管怎样，我学会了不要跟任何人谈论这件事。”袭击发生后不久，辛迪重返工作岗位，但这段经历对她产生了深远的影响。

43
00:43:28.000 --> 00:44:43.000
She became further withdrawn, and it was obvious to her co-workers that she was no longer coping with the demands of her work. She looked exhausted. The dark circles around her eyes accentuated by her pale skin. Cindy felt she had no choice but to move house again. She relocated from Vancouver to the city of Richmond, 15 kilometres south. Things settled down, and Cindy enjoyed the garden at her new rental house, a modest brown and white timber multi-leveled home. Cindy's close friends, Tom and Agnes Woodcock, came over on the night of April 12, 1986, four months after the attack in the park. They played cards and decided to stay the night, retiring to bed at 11 o'clock. At 2am, Tom heard a loud thump coming from downstairs. He was putting on his pants when Cindy knocked on his door. She had heard the same noise and asked Tom if he would go with her to investigate.
她变得更加孤僻，同事们明显看出她已经无法应对工作上的要求。她看起来筋疲力尽。苍白的皮肤衬托出她眼下的黑眼圈。辛迪觉得自己别无选择，只能再次搬家。她从温哥华搬到了南面15公里外的列治文市。情况安定下来后，辛迪很喜欢她新租的房子的花园，这是一栋朴素的棕白相间多层木结构住宅。1986年4月12日晚上，即公园袭击事件发生四个月后，辛迪的挚友汤姆和艾格尼丝·伍德科克（Tom and Agnes Woodcock）来到了她家。他们玩了牌，决定留宿，并在11点就寝。凌晨2点，汤姆听到楼下传来一声巨响。他正穿着裤子时，辛迪敲了他的房门。她听到了同样的噪音，并问汤姆是否愿意和她一起去查看。

44
00:44:43.000 --> 00:45:39.000
They made their way down the hallway together. As Tom passed the window of the living room, he could see flames coming from the basement below them. He shouted to his wife Agnes to phone for the fire brigade. Agnes soon returned, telling Tom that the phone line was dead. In response, Tom raced outside to flag down anyone who might be able to help. He saw a man in his 30s standing near Cindy's house and called to him, asking the man to phone for assistance. The man didn't reply, instead running down a side street and disappearing into the night. The fire was quickly brought under control and extinguished by the Richmond Fire Department at 2.52am.
他们一起顺着走廊走去。当汤姆经过客厅窗户时，他可以看到他们下方的地下室冒出火焰。他大声喊妻子艾格尼丝报警。艾格尼丝很快回来了，告诉汤姆电话线断了。作为回应，汤姆冲到外面去拦下任何可能提供帮助的人。他看到一个30多岁的男人站在辛迪家附近，便向他大喊，请这个人打电话求助。这个男人没有回答，而是跑进一条小巷，消失在夜色中。大火很快被列治文消防局控制并于凌晨2点52分扑灭。

45
00:45:39.000 --> 00:46:55.000
Damage was confined to the basement area and Cindy, her guests and her dog were unharmed. An investigation by authorities and a specialist fire investigator could not find any evidence to suggest who might be responsible for the blaze. Cindy thought Roy Makepeace was to blame. The fire was a massive setback to Cindy. She became increasingly despondent in the weeks that followed. The major depression that arose from Cindy, realizing that the attacks had followed her to her new place, resulted in a stay at St. Paul's Psychiatric Unit. Gradually, Cindy's mental health improved and on discharge from the hospital, she finalized her relationship with Roy Makepeace, officially divorcing in June 1986. To mark the end of the marriage, Cindy changed her surname from Makepeace to James. Rather than returning to her maiden name of Hack, Cindy liked the short, easy to remember surname of James and the new beginning at Signified.
损毁仅限于地下室区域，辛迪、她的客人和她的狗都没有受伤。当局和专业火灾调查员的调查未能找到任何证据来指明谁可能是这场火灾的负责人。辛迪认为罗伊·梅克皮斯难辞其咎。这场火灾对辛迪是一个沉重的打击。在随后的几周里，她变得越来越沮丧。辛迪意识到袭击一直追到她的新住所，由此产生的大(严重)抑郁症导致她在圣保罗精神病房住院。渐渐地，辛迪的心理健康有所改善，出院后，她终结了与罗伊·梅克皮斯的关系，于1986年6月正式离婚。为了标志这段婚姻的结束，辛迪将姓氏从梅克皮斯改为了詹姆斯（James）。辛迪没有恢复娘家姓哈克（Hack），而是喜欢简短、易记的姓氏詹姆斯以及在Signified的新开始。

46
00:46:55.000 --> 00:48:04.000
In mid-1986, Cindy went to Germany to visit and stay with her brother Roger who worked there. On return, Cindy, who had taken six months of sick leave, felt well enough to go back to work. She was immediately asked to resign. It had been decided in her absence that she wasn't coping well enough to competently continue as director of Blenheim House. The decision devastated Cindy as she lived and breathed her job. As a parting gesture, Cindy received a payout. Given that she had worked in her specialist role at Blenheim House for 13 years, the company also provided funds for Cindy to upgrade her nursing skills so she could return to work as a hospital ward nurse. Not long after, she took a job at Richmond General Hospital on award for patients who had recently been discharged from the ICU but were not well enough to return home. This job had Cindy returning to shift work and working long hours.
